Third-party notices of the mcp-registry Go image
================================================

mcp-registry itself is MIT licensed (LICENSE). This file names every third-party component the Go
image redistributes and where its licence texts are. In the image this file is
/usr/share/licenses/mcp-registry/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES; the project licence (LICENSE) and the
third_party/ directory named below are next to it, at /usr/share/licenses/mcp-registry/. In the
repository the same files are at the root and under third_party/. The generated files are made by
`go run ./tools/notices ...` (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Third-party notices"); tests in tools/notices fail
when a Go module linked into the binary is missing, or when a file no longer matches its pin.

1. Go modules compiled into /usr/local/bin/mcp-registry
   Every module the binary links (build tag onnx, linux/amd64 and linux/arm64) with the licence
   files of its module, and the licence of the Go standard library and runtime:
   third_party/go/NOTICES

2. ONNX Runtime 1.30.0 (CPU) - MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
   File: /usr/local/lib/libonnxruntime.so.1, taken unchanged from the npm package
   onnxruntime-node@1.30.0 (SHA-256 pinned in internal/modules/search/infra/onnx/native/pins.env).
   Source: https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
   Its licence and its own third-party notices (Eigen, protobuf, re2 and the other components it
   bundles), taken unchanged from the same release:
   third_party/onnxruntime/LICENSE
   third_party/onnxruntime/ThirdPartyNotices.txt
   (third_party/onnxruntime/SOURCE says where they come from and holds their SHA-256.)

3. libtokenizers.a, statically linked into the binary: github.com/daulet/tokenizers v1.27.0
   (release asset, SHA-256 pinned in pins.env; its Go module and MIT licence are in
   third_party/go/NOTICES). The Rust crates compiled into the archive, among them Hugging Face
   tokenizers 0.22.0 (Apache-2.0) and onig_sys 69.9.1 with the bundled Oniguruma (BSD-2-Clause),
   each with the licence its manifest declares and the licence files it ships:
   third_party/tokenizers/NOTICES
   Notices the generated file cannot take from licence files:
   a. esaxx-rs 0.1.10 (Apache-2.0) compiles C++ sources that carry their own MIT notices:
      sais-lite, Copyright (c) 2008-2009 Yuta Mori; esaxx, Copyright (c) 2010 Daisuke Okanohara.
   b. number_prefix 0.4.0 - MIT, Copyright (c) Benjamin Sago (the author named in its manifest;
      the crate ships no licence file).
   The MIT licence text for both follows at the end of this file.

4. Model Xenova/multilingual-e5-small (ONNX, q8), a conversion of intfloat/multilingual-e5-small
   - MIT, as both model cards declare (no copyright line is published with the model). Files under
   /app/models, downloaded at build time at a pinned revision and checked by SHA-256
   (internal/modules/search/infra/onnx/native/fetch-model.sh, pins.env).
   Source: https://huggingface.co/Xenova/multilingual-e5-small
   The MIT licence text follows at the end of this file.

5. The web UI (/app/web): the npm packages its bundle is built from (React, Base UI, TanStack
   Query, React Router, zod, lucide-react, the Inter font under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and
   the others), each with the licence its package declares and the licence files it ships:
   third_party/web/NOTICES

6. Debian packages of the base image (debian:bookworm-slim, pinned by digest) and those the image
   installs (ca-certificates, libstdc++6, tzdata): each package's copyright and licence are in the
   image at /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright, the common licence texts at
   /usr/share/common-licenses/.

